    <div class="rise">
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">01</span><span class="nm">Studio Lead</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-purple-1);color:var(--mo-purple-7)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="17"/><path d="M30 18 L26 28 L18 30 L22 20Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></span><p class="lead">Reads a brief or a screenshot and picks the route: screen, brand or audit. Does no design itself, and only proposes.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">02</span><span class="nm">Strategist</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-blue-1);color:var(--mo-blue-8)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="17"/><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="9"/><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></span><p class="lead">Goals, users and constraints, kept short, with every assumption labelled as one.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">03</span><span class="nm">UX</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-green-1);color:var(--mo-green-9)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="24" r="5"/><circle cx="38" cy="12" r="5"/><circle cx="38" cy="36" r="5"/><path d="M15 24 H24 L33 13 M24 24 L33 35"/></svg></span><p class="lead">The flow, a screen outline and every state a screen needs: first load, empty, error and success.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">04</span><span class="nm">UI</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-red-1);color:var(--mo-red-8)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="8" width="36" height="9" rx="3"/><rect x="6" y="23" width="16" height="17" rx="3"/><rect x="28" y="23" width="14" height="7" rx="3"/><rect x="28" y="33" width="14" height="7" rx="3"/></svg></span><p class="lead">Builds screens from the real Moon tokens and fixes whatever the Reviewer rejects, with the measured numbers in hand.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">05</span><span class="nm">Brand</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-yellow-1);color:var(--mo-yellow-10)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="17" cy="17" r="8"/><circle cx="32" cy="17" r="8"/><circle cx="24" cy="30" r="8"/></svg></span><p class="lead">Plans variations and sizes. An image model draws the artwork only. The studio sets every word, in Moon type.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who" name="roster"><summary><span class="n">06</span><span class="nm">Handoff</span><span class="tag ai tg2">Agent</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-orange-1);color:var(--mo-orange-8)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 14 L7 24 L17 34 M31 14 L41 24 L31 34 M27 10 L21 38"/></svg></span><p class="lead">Build specs and fix lists. For a screen, the React code is generated and then verified before you see it.</p></div></details>
      <details class="who rev" name="roster" open><summary><span class="n">07</span><span class="nm">Reviewer</span><span class="tag tg2" style="background:var(--mo-black);color:var(--mo-yellow-6)">Code, not an AI</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="body"><span class="ico" style="background:var(--mo-black);color:var(--mo-yellow-6)"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="21" cy="21" r="13"/><path d="M31 31 L42 42"/><path d="M15 21 L20 26 L28 16"/></svg></span><p class="lead">The standard keeper. Real checks in a real Chrome, rejections with numbers and fixes, and no way to talk it round.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="receipts" id="how">
  <div class="wrap stack g16">
    <div class="stack g4 rise">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Three routes, one rule</h2>
      <p class="lead">Each route plans first, shows its cost, and waits for you before it acts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cols3 rise">
      <div class="rcard"><span class="big2" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 class="h3 lg">Screens</h3>
        <ul><li>Built from the real Moon tokens, checked at three widths.</li><li>Up to three automatic fixes before you see it.</li><li>Handoff turns it into verified React.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="rcard"><span class="big2" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 class="h3 lg">Brand assets</h3>
        <ul><li>The plan shows the exact image count and cost first.</li><li>An image model draws artwork only. Chrome sets the words.</li><li>A layout fix reuses every image. Only changed looks cost more.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="rcard"><span class="big2" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 class="h3 lg">Audits</h3>
        <ul><li>A web address, an HTML file or a screenshot. It only reads.</li><li>Findings in priority order, boxed on the page, each with a fix.</li><li>Waive what is deliberate. The next audit remembers.</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stack g8 rise">
      <h3 class="h3 lg">Handoff code is checked, not trusted</h3>
      <ol class="checks">
        <li><b>1. Type check</b><span>Against Moon's real components, with Moon's own TypeScript.</span></li>
        <li><b>2. Server render</b><span>Bundled and rendered with react-dom, so it runs.</span></li>
        <li><b>3. Every word</b><span>All the text of the approved screen must be in the output.</span></li>
        <li><b>4. Rendered and reviewed</b><span>Moon's Tailwind build, a real Chrome, the same Reviewer.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GUARDRAILS + STATUS -->
<section id="status">
  <div class="wrap stack g16">
    <div class="stack g4 rise">
      <p class="eyebrow">Guardrails</p>
      <h2 class="h2">It acts for you, so the limits are deliberate</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="guardgrid rise">
      <div class="gcard gc1"><span class="w">Secrets</span><p class="small">Keys come only from environment variables and are removed from every log and message. A test fails if anything key shaped is in the source.</p></div>
      <div class="gcard gc2"><span class="w">One user</span><p class="small">The Telegram bot answers one person, by id, for messages and button presses.</p></div>
      <div class="gcard gc3"><span class="w">Money</span><p class="small">Live agents and real images are opt in, separately. A key alone never spends. Every job has a spend cap and an image cap.</p></div>
      <div class="gcard gc4"><span class="w">Read only</span><p class="small">Audits refuse private and internal addresses on every request, including redirects. No clicking, typing, signing in or downloads.</p></div>
      <div class="gcard gc5"><span class="w">Untrusted pages</span><p class="small">Text from an audited page never reaches the agent that writes the fix list. It sees counts and rule names only.</p></div>
      <div class="gcard gc6"><span class="w">Plain words</span><p class="small">Everything the studio writes is filtered for plain language, and the project is tested for it.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="stack g4 rise" style="margin-top:32px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Status</p>
      <h2 class="h2">What is proven, and what is not</h2>
      <p class="lead muted">This is a working prototype, and it says so.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tablewrap rise">
      <table>
        <caption class="skip">Status of each part</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">State</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Reviewer, gates, logging, cost caps, converter, verification, audit safety</th><td><span class="tag good">Built and tested</span> 93 automated tests, including security cases such as redirects to private addresses and a page built to bait a clicker.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">The three routes end to end</th><td><span class="tag good">Working in the demos</span> With mock agents, placeholder art and a terminal standing in for Telegram.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Real Telegram bot</th><td><span class="tag warn">Not run yet</span> Tested against a fake Telegram. Needs a bot token.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Real Claude agents</th><td><span class="tag warn">Not run yet</span> Tested against a stand in. Needs an API key.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Real Gemini images</th><td><span class="tag warn">Not run yet</span> Tested against a stand in. Needs a key, and a check of the real price per image.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="card stack g3 rise">
      <h3 class="h3">Known limits</h3>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>In demo mode the agents are templates, not a model. They answer in the same formats as the live agents, so everything around them is real.</li>
        <li>The first attempt in each demo is seeded with known flaws on purpose, so the review loop is visible.</li>
        <li>The brand artwork in the demo is placeholder art drawn in Moon colours, not generated images.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

